35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the data confirms my concern. Eleven mid-year joiners required manual calculations, and nine tasters refused annual commitments. We need flexible entry points.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, interesting, but irrelevant to my core issue. The ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. We must address the administrative burden first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, the data is stark. A quarter of members do two-thirds of the work. The same nine handle setup. We need to address this imbalance.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, that imbalance explains the hesitation. People feel the cost is unfair when they see the effort. I’ll address that in the fee structure.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, seventy percent fixed costs? That’s why the account is thin. I need to know exactly how much cash we can count on, not just the workload.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, fixed costs don’t justify opaque billing. If newcomers see a rigid annual fee, they won’t join. We need transparent, modular pricing to lower that barrier.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, transparency is fine, but it doesn’t reduce the six hours of monthly chasing. I need a collection method that minimizes that specific administrative drain.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the administrative drain is real, but the imbalance is deeper. If only nine people carry the load, a flat fee feels unjust. We must acknowledge that effort.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, chasing fees is a symptom, not the cure. If the fee feels like a penalty for showing up, you’ll chase forever. We need to fix the value perception first.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, value perception is nice, but cash is king. A third of renewals needed chasing. I need a structure that guarantees money arrives, not just feels fair.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, guaranteed cash is impossible if the entry barrier remains. We need a structure that accommodates the eleven mid-year joiners without manual calculations.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, guaranteed cash requires a method that doesn’t require six hours of monthly chasing. I need a collection system that is administratively sustainable, not just financially aggressive.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if the fee ignores the nine doing the heavy lifting, resentment grows. We need to value that effort, not just chase the money.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, resentment kills the club. If the fee feels like a tax on belonging, people vanish. We must make the value undeniable, not just the cost visible.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, chasing is a failure. I need a structure where money arrives automatically. No more manual work, no more guessing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We need a system that handles mid-year entries automatically. This reduces your administrative burden while keeping the entry barrier low for newcomers.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, automatic handling is the only logical path. If we eliminate the monthly chasing, the role becomes sustainable. I support any structure that achieves that.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We must ensure the fee structure reflects the actual effort of those nine. Let’s move to the options.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I agree. The hesitation stems from feeling like a burden. We need a structure that makes belonging effortless, not a transaction. Let’s see the options.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,I’m done arguing. I need the options that guarantee cash flow. Let’s see what we’re actually choosing.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
